    description: "WHAT, after PR #2200:\n- Top-level extension properties sit on the variable tier: `val String.tp` and `val Int.tp` share an id (MOVES IDS if fixed).\n- `_extract_kotlin_receiver_type` (meta, read by receiver_type_dispatch) returns None after modifiers and for nullable or parenthesized receivers.\n- Primary-constructor `val` / `var` parameters and secondary constructors are not symbols.\n- Context receivers do not parse; an annotation on a parenthesized or function type swallows the rest of the file (grammar).\n- Type parameters and bounds: see the cross-language type-parameter item.\n\nFound during PR 2 of the stable-id plan (the v15 bump), 2026-11-16 (PR #2200). Detail: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/pr2/STATUS.md."  # 41ac
